# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the UI tests.
#
# Leak checking is off by default; UI_TEST_LEAK_CHECK=1 turns it on. This file
# is what makes that opt-in usable, and it is deliberately almost empty.
#
# A clean startup and exit already reports 633 records and 121 KB. 344 of them
# are purely library, and the ones that name our code mostly do not mean what
# they look like: LSan blames the nearest frame that is not in a system library,
# so pango's font and shaping caches are reported against whichever of our
# functions first asked pango to lay text out. The largest single group, 101
# records, is attributed to update_tab_width() in mootextview.c, which frees all
# three of the things it allocates.
#
# So suppressing by the name of the function a leak is blamed on would suppress
# the next real leak in that same function, which is the opposite of what a
# suppression file is for. Entries here should name the library that actually
# retains the memory, not the frame of ours it is charged to.
#
# Syntax: one "leak:<substring of a frame>" per line.

# Fontconfig builds its pattern and charset caches on first use and keeps them
# for the life of the process by design.
leak:libfontconfig
